  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening anti-poaching operations to protect elephant in Chuilexi Conservancy, Niassa Reserve, Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to strengthen protection and anti-poaching for elephants in the Chuilexi area of the Niassa area in northern Mozambique. Elephants in Niassa are under severe threat and now number fewer than 2,000 (&lt;10% of the population ten years ago). In addition to protecting elephants, this project also benefits all of Niassas wildlife, including important populations of lions and buffalo. This proposal is for a twelve-month period. Objectives include strengthening anti-poaching efforts (through provision of new uniforms and supplies for 62 scouts and equipping patrol teams with handheld radios), improving coverage and response rate of anti-poaching patrols during the wet season (by procuring a patrol boat and initiating water-based patrols on the Lugenda River), and supporting the canine unit (through training for dogs and handlers and operational expenses for deployments).</narrative>
  </description>
